  'help.6': '<b>Draw</b> (toolbar on the canvas): line <kbd>L</kbd>, polyline <kbd>P</kbd>, rectangle <kbd>B</kbd>, circle <kbd>O</kbd>, dimension <kbd>D</kbd>, text <kbd>T</kbd>, back to select <kbd>V</kbd>/<kbd>Esc</kbd>. Points snap to the grid, to corners and to track ends. While drawing, type a length in mm (rectangle: <code>2400x1200</code>) and press <kbd>Enter</kbd>; <kbd>Shift</kbd> locks to 15° steps. Select a single drawing to drag its corner handles; double-click text to edit it.',
  'help.7': '<b>Rectangle size:</b> mark a rectangle and type Size X / Size Y in the panel at the top right (<kbd>Enter</kbd> jumps into it). Drag a side line to change only the size in that direction, drag a corner to change both (it stays a rectangle), drag inside a marked rectangle to move it. Its dimensions follow.',
  'help.8': '<b>Save</b> (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>S</kbd>) writes to the file the layout was opened from or last saved to; <b>Save as…</b> (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>S</kbd>) chooses a new file. <b>Open…</b> (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd>) loads a file. Dialogs start in the data folder from the settings (⚙). Browsers other than Chrome/Edge can only download, so there Save works like Save as…. Your current work is also kept automatically between sessions.',
